    "updated_at": "2026-11-26T21:49:30Z",
    "body": "**SF32: not in the first slice. Some numbers are missing.**\n\nThe link to `Maschinenzubehoer_2611.pdf` in the comment above now gives a 404 error. The current catalog is at:\nhttps://www.fehlmann.com/fileadmin/redakteur/06_PDF_Zertifikate/PDF/Maschinenzubehoer.pdf\n\nNumbers that we have:\n- From qsmits's STEP (the taper only), in mm:\n  - The large end of the taper is Ø30.8 at the top face.\n  - The taper half angle is approximately 7.6 degrees.\n  - The groove is Ø20.6, from 12.4 to 16.7 below the top face. Its flanks are at 45 degrees.\n  - The drive dog is Ø18 with flats 9.4 apart, from 42.5 to 54.25 below the top face.\n- From the catalog, pages 21-22:\n  - ER11 nut Ø19, L 40 / 70.\n  - ER16 nut Ø28, L 45 / 75.\n  - ER25 nut Ø42, L 32 to 110.\n  - ER32 nut Ø49.5, L 44.\n  - Weldon chucks: D2 25 to 52, L 27 to 46.\n\nNumbers that are missing:\n1. The diameter and the length of the shoulder below the large end of the taper. This is the steel between the spindle face and the holder body. The catalog drawings do not give it, and the STEP does not include it.\n2. The datum face of the catalog dimension L. On the ER drawings, L starts at the large end of the taper. On the Weldon drawing, L starts at the back face of the body, below the shoulder. We must know from which face each L starts.\n3. The position of the spindle face on the holder: does the top face of the taper (Ø30.8) align with the spindle face?\n\nThese numbers set the outline below the spindle face. The collision checks use that outline, so we do not guess them. A caliper measurement of one ER holder and one Weldon holder is sufficient: the shoulder Ø and length, and the length from the spindle face to the nose.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
